; Singularity VR mod - settings
;
; [Render] ResX / ResY force the game's backbuffer size.
;
; With true stereo (F1) the frame is side by side, so each eye gets ResX/2 x ResY.
; The headset wants roughly 2496x2688 per eye, so matching it means ResX ~= 4992.
;
; Why this matters: at the default 2560x1440 each eye is only 1280x1440, which is
; about 14 pixels per degree at full FOV against the headset's ~25. That
; undersampling, upscaled to fill the eye, is what makes textures shimmer.
;
; Cost: the frame copy is still a CPU round-trip, so pixels are expensive until
; the D3D9Ex zero-copy path lands. Expect the frame rate to drop as this goes up.
;
; Suggested ladder - try these in order and watch both sharpness and fps:
;   3200x1800   per eye 1600x1800   ~1.6x the pixels
;   3840x2160   per eye 1920x2160   ~2.3x
;   4992x2688   per eye 2496x2688   ~3.6x, matches the headset
;
; Set both to 0 (or delete them) to leave the game's own resolution alone.

[Render]
ResX=3840
ResY=2160
